Coming to the charge under Section 304-B of IPC, before a person can be convicted under this Section, which deals with what is described as 1. Hansraj Sharma and others v. State Govt. of NCT of Delhi, 175(2010) DLT 446,
decided on 02.03.2010 State v. Niranjan Kumar & others "dowry death , the prosecution must necessarily prove the following ingredients:-
i. The death of a woman must have been caused by burn or bodily injury or otherwise than under normal circumstance;
ii. Such death must have occurred within seven years of her marriage;
iii. Soon before her death, the woman must have been subjected to cruelty or harassment by her husband or by relatives of her husband;
